{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"ls; rg -n 'compile-guest-call|call-entry|no carrier' . --glob '\"'!collab/**'\"' | head -80; git branch -a | head -50\"","aggregated_output":"AGENTS.md\nBRIEF-j6g-fix.md\nCLAUDE.md\nDUPLICATE-DISPATCH-aaq.md\nGEMINI.md\nLICENSE\nLICENSE-EXCEPTION\nREADME.md\nVERIFICATION-aaq.md\nanalysis_options.yaml\nandroid\nantlr\nassets\nbb.edn\nbin\nbuild\ncollab\nconfig.clj\ndemo\ndemo_yang.clj\ndeps.edn\ndocker\ndocs\nexamples\nios\njolt-toolchain.edn\nlib\nlinux\nmacos\nmise.toml\nnative\nnginx.conf\norchestrator-logs\npackage-lock.json\npackage.json\npublic\npubspec.lock\npubspec.yaml\nshadow-cljs.edn\nsrc\ntarget\ntest\ntest.sh\ntools\nvllm.sh\nweb\nwindows\nx\n./public/chp/blog/hygienic-parallel-transport-universal-continuation-format.blog:336:           \"A continuation is a value, not a session. That is the stance at the head of the UCF specification, and everything else follows from taking it seriously. A value can be content-addressed, so it can be deduplicated and verified. A value can be carried by anything, so no carrier is privileged. A value can be read by anyone, so custody must be arbitrated above the carrier by a boundary that actually possesses something. Hygiene makes the value mean the same thing everywhere. The lease makes sure it runs in only one place at a time. Between them, a suspended computation becomes a vector in a bundle over the distributed world, and UCF is the connection that lets it travel.\"]\n./orchestrator-logs/1793292851-yang-python-retake.md:153:  python-s3-wiring (10 files: call.cljc, lower.cljc, prelude.cljc, the call-entry fixture, the\n./orchestrator-logs/1793292851-yang-python-retake.md:221:  call-entry/call/publication/gate-test all green, the generator byte-identical. The dao.stream\n./orchestrator-logs/1793292851-yang-python-retake.md:485:  - the pysweep jupiter results (call-entry, safepoint, import namespaces)\n./orchestrator-logs/1793385006-zcode-glm-5.3-flash-yang-clojure-track.md:46:Done: (1) Re-derived the 33-failure regression on the clean rebased tree: bracket GREEN at the rebase base 0dc5d7af (118/0, adoption included), RED from 211dded9 onward — the gate-closure round was authored on the PRE-adoption base and its self-reported green predates the merge. (2) Root cause, measured by probes on both trees: the round introduced a parallel invoker convention — `fn?` stripped of its `yang.call/eligible?` fallback (so `(fn? first)`=false for §8.10 descriptor maps), and a library `invoke-value` (bare `data/callable?` classification → map-lookup branch) wired to a fast path routing ALL local/non-symbol calls through it, so `(f 41)` on a local silently returned nil (get-fallback) and destructuring/update/apply misfired (the 33). (3) Reconciliation (uncommitted): compile-guest-call routes entry-PRESENT callees through admission (admitted→bridged, forged→refused) and entry-ABSENT callees (collections, raw closures) to invoke-value — itself invoked as a proper common call (yang.call/invoke + escape-based raise mirroring bridged's capture/resume); `fn?` restored to the adoption definition; `::invoker` detection tightened to the invoke-value name; the gate round's try/->/fresh-supply/kind-seam work kept. (4) astra r1 (thread 01a199e5) DENIED with two P2 blockers: dispatcher re-entry (apply inside invoke-value recursed into the routing → 30k-instruction exhaustion on scalar/raw-closure callees) and the entry test checking truthiness not presence (`{:yang.call/entry nil}` would lookup). (5) v2: invoke-value refuses via `(throw (yang.call/condition :yang.call/not-callable {...}))` (no apply anywhere), routing test is map-guarded key presence (`(if (data/map? c) (data/contains? c :yang.call/entry) false)`), and new `test-value-invocation-refusals-are-terminating` (library-enabled, walker+semantic): scalar exact-shape refusal, module-fn admission (measured: the linker compiles module fns as ADMITTED descriptors — `(yang.call/entry f)` legitimately succeeds; the projected raw closure refuses), nil/false entry presence refusals, tail-position refusal, operands-before-check in both positions via a guest throw (native refusals escape as host exceptions outside adapter seams — probed and discarded). Focused lane 122/0; kondo 0/0 both files.\n./orchestrator-logs/1793385006-zcode-glm-5.3-flash-yang-clojure-track.md:486:Done: (1) Fix r3 (d3a35830) was remote-verified GREEN on jupiter (matrix 13/18/0, yang.base 122/0) — the round's claims accurate. (2) The FINAL codex gate REJECTED on the substantive core: the fallback keys on the map SHAPE, but genuine references are ISSUED AS MAPS by the VM (engine.cljc:316) with exactly {:type :cell-ref :id :seal} — authenticity lives in the heap+seal check, not the shape. A full-shape three-entry data map (with any 64-char seal string) still routes to admission and fails at cell/get instead of doing its map lookup. The r3 tests cover only NON-matching shapes (four entries, three-char seal) — neither exercises the matching shape; the \"runtime-built\" case is a bound literal. The seal prevents capability bypass; it does not restore ordinary map semantics. (3) Real fix direction (now precise): route shape-matching maps to admission as required for genuine references, but FALL BACK to plain map invocation specifically when authenticity fails (invalid seal / nonexistent cell = never genuine = it is data); genuine-but-dead references must keep the current refusal (the D2 witness bar intact). (4) Second blocker surfaced by the gate: merge-base d3a35830/8fb525c4 = 7eb7fc9e — the branch does NOT contain the landed D2, and both lanes changed clojure.cljc (call-entry/admission/preamble vs routing/globals/run-main). Landing requires a REBASE with conflict reconciliation between the token-packet lane and the runtime-module lane, then re-verification of the merge result — the quoted checks do not by themselves establish the merge behavior. (5) DELEGATE DISCIPLINE: the cell-ref map-semantics defect has now failed TWO consecutive fix rounds (r2 left the presence-key residual; r3 fixed the wrong side of it). Roster allows a different model; rather than a third same-model round, the unit is STOPPED per the delegate-death rule and escalated to the user.\n./docs/slice9-h3-1-blocked-fixtures.md:173:  - Frames `7..9`: `compile-guest-call` escape bridge (`[... coll f res s val dsg__loop0 dsg__raise_escape]`) inside `yang/library` `reduce`/`map` -> `call-entry` (`[dsg__body dsg__invocation ...]`).\n./docs/slice9-h3-1-blocked-fixtures.md:216:  - **Continuation Stack**: Depth **`32`** (`{:eval-operand 31, :eval-operator 1}`). Frames alternate between `dsg__assoc` (`[k k2 k3 m v v2 v3]`), `call-entry` (`[dsg__body dsg__invocation ...]`), `compile-guest-call` escape bridges (`[... dsg__callee dsg__arguments dsg__raise_escape]`), and `gate-nbe-evaluation` / `gate-typing-type-of-term` (`[ctx def-env fn-env t]`, `[ctx def-env ty x]`).\n./docs/slice9-h3-1-blocked-fixtures.md:248:  - **At `4M`**: `1,120 / 2,360` calls (`47.46%`), continuation depth `30` (`{:eval-operand 30}`), control `{:type :if}` inside `call-entry` (`[dsg__body dsg__invocation ...]`), inside second `:have <b>`'s `[gate-norm-beta-eq? 4]` (call `#1106` at step `3,974,712`).\n./docs/slice9-h3-1-blocked-fixtures.md:256:  - **Continuation Stack**: Depth **`23`** (`{:return 23}`). Active call chain alternates cleanly between kernel functions (`gate-typing-type-of-term`, `gate-typing-type-of-app`, `gate-proof-elab-have-impl`, `gate-proof-elab-have`, `gate-proof-elab-proof-step`, `gate-proof-elab-proof`, `gate-proof-check-proof`) and the shared descriptor wrapper `call-entry` (`entry = 454`, return `pc = 511`).\n./docs/slice9-h3-1-blocked-fixtures.md:332:| **`call-entry` (`PC 454` + `[dsg__entry_outcome]` `PC 668`)** (`clojure.cljc:1055–1097`) | `76,917` (`6.48%`) | **`325,443` (`6.50%`)** | Shared descriptor entry wrapper checking `:clj/outcome-token`, `:yang.call/named`, and unwrapping `[:yin.k/ok v]` |\n./docs/slice9-h3-1-blocked-fixtures.md:341:| **Subtotal — Static Prelude (`PC 0..850`) Alone** | **`974,883` (`82.16%`)** | **`4,083,545` (`81.52%`)** | Before counting per-call-site `compile-guest-call` bridges (`u/capture`, `raise` closure, arg vector, `bind-outcome`)! |\n./docs/slice9-h3-1-blocked-fixtures.md:342:| **Per-Call-Site `compile-guest-call` + `bind-outcome` Bridges** | `~160,781` (`13.55%`) | **`~681,091` (`13.60%`)** | `8,259` `:current-continuation` ops, `raise` closures, `[:yin.k/ok v]` re-wrap & `bind-outcome` unwrap |\n./docs/slice9-h3-1-blocked-fixtures.md:389:   On every non-tail call (`8,259` calls in `:check-assume-have-discharge`), `compile-guest-call` captures the current continuation (`u/capture`) and allocates a `raise` escape closure so `yang.call/invoke` can return a bare value; inside `call-entry` (`lines 1077–1080`), the callee's `[:yin.k/ok v]` outcome is unwrapped to `v`, returned through `yang.call/invoke`, and **immediately re-wrapped** into `[:yin.k/ok v]` at `line 1232` (`(outcome-node ok-tag (u/v result))`), only for the caller's `bind-outcome` to unwrap `[:yin.k/ok v]` a second time! (Tail calls already pass `:clj/outcome-token` to forward outcomes without unwrapping; non-tail calls do not.)\n./src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc:2469:   restore (step 12), which therefore meets no carrier defect. Answers the\n./docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1958:counter `max(local, carried)` for ordinary resume. Restore meets no carrier\n./docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2306:   (2026-10-13)**, codex D4 by R6: the earlier phrase \"is no carrier\n./docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2980:| D4 | §4.2, §7.2, §8.3 item 6 | a primitive is an admitted carrier value; the register kernel refuses one in its payload `:yin.k/unsupported :continuation-registers` with the path before attach; \"is no carrier value\" withdrawn; four refusal fixtures | engineer deviation 8, codex D4: the limit is the receiver's, not the carrier's |\n./src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1178:(defn- call-entry\n./src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1382:(defn- compile-guest-call\n./src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1457:    (compile-guest-call (compile-form f false env macro-env)\n./src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1553:    (compile-guest-call (compile-form operator false env macro-env)\n./src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:2382:           (outcomes? env) (u/let1 'dsg__make_entry (call-entry))\n./test/yang/python/antlr/call_entry_test.cljc:1:(ns yang.python.antlr.call-entry-test\n  agent.tzu.postgraphics\n+ ble-track2\n  c4-i5\n  c4-i6\n  c4-i6-r4\n+ callsite-contract-clojure\n+ callsite-ts-adoption\n+ cc2-transform-session-c1\n  cc3-lowering-provenance\n  dao.stream-redesign\n  dao.stream.whatsapp\n  dht-import-regen-test\n  exception-js-r1r3\n+ exception-php-r1r2r3\n  exception-py-r2r3\n  exception-r0\n+ exception-r3\n* exception-r3-impl\n  f1-importers-diagnosis\n  f1-importers-diagnosis-r2\n+ f12-diagnosis-fixes\n  feat/p1-forward-fixes\n  feat/p5-oracle-recording\n+ feat/p5b2-lifecycle\n+ feat/p5b2-oracle-promotion\n+ feat/p8-legacy-retirement\n  feat/prelude-tree-balance\n+ feat/roundB1-p9-contracts\n  fix/dart-cljd-compile-guards\n+ fix/exception-kit-donor-publication\n  h3-2-integration\n+ j6g-mob-astra\n+ j6g-mob-ds\n+ j6g-mob-qwen\n+ jolt-j4d-fixes\n+ jolt-j5\n+ jolt-j6f\n+ jolt-j6g\n+ jolt-orch2\n+ master\n  nightly-reds-fix\n+ py-step7-followups\n+ python-golden-remint\n  python-s1-entry\n+ roundC-p9-fixtures\n  s11-python-legs\n+ wp-w0a\n  yang-common-call\n  yang-designs-reconciled\n+ yang-php-math-fixes\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
