ofile 'dsg__provenance\ntest/yang/call/python_exception_test.clj:35:  (let [private-names '#{dsg__condition-exception cell/dsg__new-provenance\ntest/yang/call/python_exception_test.clj:36:                         cell/dsg__provenance}\ntest/yang/call/python_exception_test.clj:140:                       :provenance (list 'cell/dsg__provenance 'exception)})))\ntest/yang/python/antlr/call_entry_test.cljc:1:(ns yang.python.antlr.call-entry-test\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/state.md:123:**Provenance:** an entry may carry an optional private `:provenance` sibling beside `:value` and `:seal`, written only by the privileged mint (`cell/dsg__new-provenance`, effect `:cell/new-provenance`) at allocation, never attached, replaced, or cleared afterwards. The VM treats it as opaque data — no frontend dispatch, no reason matching, no rendering — and answers it only through the authenticated private reader (`cell/dsg__provenance`, effect `:cell/provenance`), which returns nil for anything else and is never fatal. `cell/get` returns only `:value`; `cell/set!` and `heap-write` preserve `:provenance` while updating `:value`/`:seal`. The collector traces `:provenance` as data from every live entry, from pinned entries, and as an extra root at allocation, so payload cells referenced only by a retained provenance stay reachable while the wrapper is, and become collectible when the wrapper drops.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
